From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UefiBootManagerLib: trace each handle ConnectAll visits

Diagnostic only. BDS stops making progress inside
PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole's BootDiscoveryPolicyHandler: the boot prompt
prints, EfiBootManagerConnectAll starts its walk over 296 handles, and
ConnectController on the third one never returns. Nothing else is emitted
afterwards -- a busy ConnectController would still be installing protocols --
so it is blocked rather than working.

Log the handle and its device path before each ConnectController, so the last
line printed is the controller that did not return, by construction. The
early handles carry no device path, so also list the protocols each one
produces: that set is what decides which driver bindings ConnectController
will offer the handle to, and therefore which Supported() or Start() is the
one that hangs.

DEBUG_ERROR so it survives whatever the platform sets
PcdDebugPrintErrorLevel to, and inside DEBUG_CODE so a RELEASE build is
untouched. The protocol listing is verbose for a healthy walk, but a walk
that stalls on the third handle only ever emits a dozen lines. Drop this
patch once the offending controller is identified.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmConnect.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmConnect.c
@@ -38,6 +38,49 @@
            );
 
     for (Index = 0; Index < HandleCount; Index++) {
+      DEBUG_CODE_BEGIN ();
+      CHAR16    *BmDpText;
+      EFI_GUID  **BmProtocols;
+      UINTN     BmProtocolCount;
+      UINTN     BmProtoIdx;
+
+      BmDpText = ConvertDevicePathToText (
+                   DevicePathFromHandle (HandleBuffer[Index]),
+                   FALSE,
+                   FALSE
+                   );
+      DEBUG ((
+        DEBUG_ERROR,
+        "BmConnectAll[%u/%u]: handle %p %s\n",
+        (UINT32)Index,
+        (UINT32)HandleCount,
+        HandleBuffer[Index],
+        (BmDpText == NULL) ? L"<no device path>" : BmDpText
+        ));
+      if (BmDpText != NULL) {
+        FreePool (BmDpText);
+      }
+
+      //
+      // Early handles carry no device path, so the text above cannot name
+      // them. List what they produce instead -- that is what decides which
+      // driver bindings ConnectController will try.
+      //
+      if (!EFI_ERROR (
+            gBS->ProtocolsPerHandle (
+              HandleBuffer[Index],
+              &BmProtocols,
+              &BmProtocolCount
+              )))
+      {
+        for (BmProtoIdx = 0; BmProtoIdx < BmProtocolCount; BmProtoIdx++) {
+          DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "    proto %g\n", BmProtocols[BmProtoIdx]));
+        }
+
+        FreePool (BmProtocols);
+      }
+
+      DEBUG_CODE_END ();
       gBS->ConnectController (HandleBuffer[Index], NULL, NULL, TRUE);
     }
 
